From 237ee79d69993046c3154c4f7b702abaf846a848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:48:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] autotests: Published EDIDs of other USB-C glasses come up
 by their identity

mockGlassesTest reads the EDIDs other owners published for their glasses
(autotests/integration/data/*.hex, each source in usb-c-glasses-edids.txt):
the VITURE Pro XR (CVT 0x3132) and the XREAL Air 2 Pro (MRG 0x3135) in 2D
and in Full SBS, where they keep their identity and announce one 3840x1080
at 60 Hz; the XREAL Air, Nreal Light, VITURE Beast, Rokid Air, Rokid Max
and the TCL SmartGlasses 0x03D4 and 0x03D5, whose 2D EDID only is public;
and two controls, a 32:9 monitor and an ordinary monitor with the PnP ID
MRG. Known glasses have their option on; Full SBS comes up as the side by
side (full) twin; a 2D mode stays as it is; the controls stay 2D.
Both measured pairs follow their glasses from 2D to Full SBS and back.

Queue row 132.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
